WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.711
- OK, numerous nights and days

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:04.045
that you think about leaving the bubble.

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:05.922
I think everyone has, including you guys.

00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:07.132
- [Laughing]

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:08.425
- [Reporter:] Well, I'm
being serious.

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:09.259
- Well, I'm just saying,

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:11.845
I don't think there's not one
person that has not had a mind

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.597
that says, “Oh, I gotta
get the hell out of here.”

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:15.974
- That bus ain’t left?

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:17.684
- It's gone.
- Fuck!

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.518
Man.

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:24.649
- [Laughing]

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:27.110
- Oh, thank you. You talk to Callie?

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.154
- I did! I said, I was like,

00:00:29.154 --> 00:00:30.572
“Are you gonna come to the bubble?”

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:31.406
But she's not.

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:33.366
- Oh no, I was telling her she
is not coming to the bubble.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.201
We’re gonna make sure of it.
- She's on vacation.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:39.539
- [Announcer:] Welcome to
Orlando. The local time is 10:33.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.041
- Good shit.
- Thank you.

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:45.045
- Hey, Tacko. [Laughing]
Thank you.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.629
- I had to bring it out.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:49.132
- OK, so while I'm waiting for sound,

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:51.342
I'm trying to draft my fantasy team.

00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:53.344
This is multitasking in the bubble.

00:01:00.852 --> 00:01:03.396
So, I have been in the
bubble since July 12.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.232
There have been good moments, bad moments,

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.068
lonely moments, happy moments.

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:11.529
It's just been a big
roller coaster of emotions.

00:01:11.529 --> 00:01:15.200
But we are now here, and it is the start

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.410
of Round 2 of the NBA playoffs

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.999
[Crowd cheering]

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:25.668
- [Announcer:] Dunk’s good, Butler.

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:28.421
[Crowd:] Defense! Defense!

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.764
- Last night, the Miami Heat
got a huge win over Giannis

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:38.723
and the Milwaukee Bucks.

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:41.518
So it's only right we go
check out their practice.

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:46.523
- [Players talking]

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.028
- [Taylor:] You.
- Well, obviously me, but—

00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:52.862
- [Taylor:] You. Oooh,

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:54.197
drop the skincare routine.

00:01:55.907 --> 00:01:58.076
[Laughing]
- I’m just sayin’, hey.

00:01:58.076 --> 00:01:59.410
Hey, don't gas me.

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:02.330
- He better make these.

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:05.917
[Crowd cheering]

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:12.423
Oh, my God.
[Laughing]

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:15.135
- [Whistling]

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.344
You healthy, so we don't gotta worry

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:17.512
about no heart attacks.

00:02:19.097 --> 00:02:22.142
- Coach!
X! Run X!

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:22.976
- Huh?

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:25.061
- [Man:] Good job, men.

00:02:25.061 --> 00:02:27.814
- Good shit, bro.
- [Clapping]

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.482
- Andy, man, why you hiding, eh?

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.608
- Oh, yeah, Andy, what up?

00:02:30.608 --> 00:02:33.361
What up, Andy?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:37.657
- Thanks for giving us all a heart attack.

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:43.079
- You know, whenever you have that,

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:45.039
you can't key in on just one guy.

00:02:45.039 --> 00:02:46.040
We got so many guys that

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.458
are constantly working on their game.

00:02:47.458 --> 00:02:49.544
They get to pick and choose their spots.

00:02:49.544 --> 00:02:51.754
You know, Duncan was huge for us.

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:53.381
Bam was huge for us.
- No—

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:55.091
- Tyler, Goran.

00:02:55.091 --> 00:02:56.676
- Can you hurry it up? My back hurts.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:58.094
- I'm trying. What—

00:02:58.094 --> 00:02:59.846
Well, if you wouldn’t do that, your back won’t hurt.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.848
- [Laughing]
- I'm just saying.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:04.559
[Crowd cheering]

00:03:21.492 --> 00:03:26.497
[Whistle blowing]

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:28.666
- If Tacko Fall touches this ball—

00:03:28.666 --> 00:03:30.210
- He's gettin' a piece of this.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.044
- [Laughing]
- No, no, no—

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:33.338
- He's getting a piece of this.
- The hoop, you big goof!

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:36.925
The hoop.
[Buzzer]

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:37.842
- Oh, shtuff!

00:03:39.093 --> 00:03:41.554
- Oh, did he make it?

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.766
- No! He made it!

00:03:44.766 --> 00:03:45.600
- Did he make it?

00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:47.477
- What?!

00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:50.688
No!

00:03:50.688 --> 00:03:52.023
- Oh, you're lyin'!

00:03:52.023 --> 00:03:53.316
It didn't count, did it?

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.319
- No, they gotta, they gotta review that.

00:03:56.319 --> 00:03:58.780
I don't think that counts.
- No, 0.5!

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.031
- I don't think that counts.

00:04:00.031 --> 00:04:00.823
- No!

00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:02.659
- Watch, watch.

00:04:05.036 --> 00:04:08.539
[Gasping] It did! it did!

00:04:08.539 --> 00:04:11.376
- Hey, yo!
- He released it before.

00:04:15.338 --> 00:04:17.507
I am so happy you brought the kids, Fred.

00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:19.133
- Hi, Sanaa.

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:20.510
- Yeah, daddy-daughter day.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:21.928
- Hello!
- Say hi.

00:04:23.221 --> 00:04:24.055
- Hi.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.685
I love your pink dress. It's so cute!

00:04:30.853 --> 00:04:32.105
[Laughing]

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:35.024
- Can you ask her, say “What's your name?”

00:04:35.024 --> 00:04:36.442
No, your name is Sanaa.
- Sanaa?

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:37.485
You can come in.

00:04:37.485 --> 00:04:38.820
- What's her name?

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:39.654
Watch the cord.

00:04:39.654 --> 00:04:42.323
- You wanna be
in the interview, Sanaa?

00:04:42.323 --> 00:04:43.157
[Laughing]

00:04:43.157 --> 00:04:44.784
- With Doritos on your face?

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:45.618
- Yeah!

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:46.619
- Lemme see.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.746
- Oh, she's precious.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.083
- Shelby got you—

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:54.043
got Doritos all on your face?
- Mmhmm.

00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.795
- Your mama's gonna kill
me. You know that, right?

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:56.629
- [Laughing]

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.132
Well, I'm just gonna
say that at this point,

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:02.343
the playoff Raptors are pretty
synonymous with clutch shots.

00:05:02.343 --> 00:05:03.428
- Yeah.
- Wouldn't you say?

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:04.762
- Yeah, for sure, luckily.

00:05:04.762 --> 00:05:06.222
- Yeah, luckily, absolutely.

00:05:06.222 --> 00:05:08.933
I mean, Kawhi's four-bounce game-winner,

00:05:08.933 --> 00:05:10.768
OG's big shot in Game 3.

00:05:10.768 --> 00:05:13.313
I mean, what are the
similarities that you saw

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.522
between those two shots?

00:05:15.773 --> 00:05:18.359
- Crazy shots that nobody
thought were going in.

00:05:18.359 --> 00:05:20.737
Last-second buzzer-beaters
in the playoffs are,

00:05:20.737 --> 00:05:21.571
you know, kinda rare.

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:23.573
I know it doesn't seem that
way now, being in a bubble,

00:05:23.573 --> 00:05:26.159
but historically, it seems rare,

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.285
and you don't see many of 'em,

00:05:27.285 --> 00:05:29.495
so I'm just glad to be a part of both.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.831
And if you wanna keep
advancing this time of year,

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.082
you gotta have some of those.

00:05:33.082 --> 00:05:35.293
- Yeah. I mean, you talk
about being a part of both.

00:05:35.293 --> 00:05:37.128
It's kinda crazy cuz you were actually

00:05:37.128 --> 00:05:40.673
the primary option on OG’s game-winner.
- Yeah.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.800
- I mean, how was it supposed to play out?

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.802
- Yeah. Well, in a perfect world,

00:05:44.802 --> 00:05:47.472
I would have ran right to the
ball, caught it and shot it.

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:49.474
But, you know, I was able
to draw a little attention,

00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:51.768
and I think they fell asleep a little bit,

00:05:51.768 --> 00:05:53.478
and OG stepped up and knocked it down.

00:05:53.478 --> 00:05:55.897
So, that was big for us, for sure.

00:05:55.897 --> 00:05:58.107
- OK, the matchup we wanted to see,

00:05:58.107 --> 00:06:02.570
Lakers taking on the Rockets.
Headed to that game right now.

00:06:03.946 --> 00:06:06.783
[Crowd cheering]

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:08.868
- [Announcer:] Three-point basket, Harden.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:12.288
[Intense dramatic music]

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:27.595
[Whistle blowing]

00:06:27.845 --> 00:06:30.098
[Clapping]

00:06:31.474 --> 00:06:34.811
- This Lakers-Rockets Game
1 gettin' a little chippy.

00:06:34.811 --> 00:06:38.314
I think we might see a
brawl or two—not a brawl,

00:06:38.314 --> 00:06:41.818
but it's gonna be very aggressive,
this series, I can tell.

00:06:41.818 --> 00:06:45.363
[Crowd cheering]

00:06:45.363 --> 00:06:47.782
[Whistle blowing]

00:06:47.782 --> 00:06:49.742
Leaving the Raptors-Celtics game.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.828
I checked the score for Clippers-Nuggets,

00:06:51.828 --> 00:06:55.123
and the Nuggets are up
45-24, end of the first.

00:06:55.123 --> 00:06:56.249
Gotta go.

00:06:56.249 --> 00:07:01.254
[Intense dramatic music]

00:07:07.468 --> 00:07:09.220
- [Announcer:] Nikola Jokic.

00:07:12.306 --> 00:07:14.559
[Whistle blowing]

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:19.772
- We are goin' to overtime!

00:07:22.066 --> 00:07:24.819
[Crowd:] Defense! Defense!

00:07:27.989 --> 00:07:32.994
[Whistle blowing]

00:07:34.745 --> 00:07:35.580
- [Announcer:] Threeeee!

00:07:44.672 --> 00:07:46.048
[Players shouting]

00:07:46.048 --> 00:07:48.301
[Clapping]

00:07:50.219 --> 00:07:52.388
- [Announcer:] Anthony Davis!

00:07:54.265 --> 00:07:58.603
- OK, definitely been
a rough, like, 24 hours.

00:07:58.603 --> 00:08:01.814
Rough time while I'm here in the bubble.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:04.525
My great uncle passed away.

00:08:04.525 --> 00:08:05.818
For those of you that don't know,

00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:09.238
Lou Brock is my great uncle.

00:08:09.238 --> 00:08:12.366
He was a Hall of Famer with
the St. Louis Cardinals.

00:08:12.366 --> 00:08:15.995
One of the best to ever play the game.

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:20.249
But for me, I just lost
somebody that I love dearly.

00:08:20.249 --> 00:08:24.003
And one of the best people
that you will ever meet

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.379
in your life.

00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:29.050
He is kind and genuine
and funny and caring

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.260
and made every single
person that he came across

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:33.888
feel like the most important
person in the world.

00:08:33.888 --> 00:08:35.389
And while I know some people believe

00:08:35.389 --> 00:08:36.933
that his gift was baseball,

00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:39.477
I think that was his actual gift:

00:08:39.477 --> 00:08:44.482
making all people feel
seen and heard and amazing.

00:08:45.733 --> 00:08:47.735
He really did have a knack for that.

00:08:47.735 --> 00:08:49.237
But, yeah, so that is what's going on

00:08:49.237 --> 00:08:50.363
with me here in the bubble.

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:55.368
Definitely been a rough,
rough, rough time.

00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:57.370
But one thing that really
did lift my spirits

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.456
was seeing Jayson Tatum,
who is from St. Louis.

00:09:00.456 --> 00:09:03.626
He was wearing his Cardinal Jordan 34s.

00:09:03.626 --> 00:09:05.294
And he wrote "RIP Lou Brock."

00:09:07.088 --> 00:09:08.798
- Obviously, everybody knows he played

00:09:08.798 --> 00:09:10.174
for the St. Louis Cardinals.

00:09:11.342 --> 00:09:14.262
One of the best players ever in MLB.

00:09:14.262 --> 00:09:17.557
One of the best players
to play for the Cardinals.

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:19.809
I'm 22. I never even got to see him play,

00:09:19.809 --> 00:09:21.394
but I know what he means
to that organization

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.145
and to the city of St. Louis.

00:09:24.689 --> 00:09:29.694
And I had the Cardinal
Jordan 34s that I designed,

00:09:30.486 --> 00:09:31.487
I had those on today.

00:09:31.487 --> 00:09:33.864
And unfortunately, he
passed away yesterday, so,

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:38.661
I just wanted to shed some light on that

00:09:38.661 --> 00:09:39.829
for all the people back home.

00:09:39.829 --> 00:09:40.913
- Amen, that warmed my heart,

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:42.999
cuz I know my uncle would've loved 'em.

00:09:42.999 --> 00:09:44.625
I loved them.

00:09:44.625 --> 00:09:47.003
And, yeah, so that was a little,

00:09:47.003 --> 00:09:51.924
that was a little light in
a dark, dark couple days.

00:09:54.885 --> 00:09:58.139
- You all right?
- Yeah, I'm OK.

00:09:58.139 --> 00:10:00.391
[Shouting]

00:10:09.066 --> 00:10:13.237
[Shouting]
[Cheering]

00:10:13.237 --> 00:10:17.992
OK, not only are the Nuggets
winning over the Clippers,

00:10:17.992 --> 00:10:22.997
Michael Porter Jr. had one
of best dunks, huge poster.

00:10:23.831 --> 00:10:27.918
[Chanting and cheering]

00:10:27.918 --> 00:10:30.129
[Whistling blowing]

00:10:30.129 --> 00:10:32.381
Hey, Lou. So at a lot of these games,

00:10:32.381 --> 00:10:33.633
obviously people have family here,

00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:35.676
but it seems like you
all have a big family section.

00:10:35.676 --> 00:10:38.137
I  can hear them a
little more than the others.

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:39.889
How does it affect the way you guys play?

00:10:39.889 --> 00:10:41.891
Can you hear them the same as we can?

00:10:41.891 --> 00:10:44.393
- It's just good to have
a support system here

00:10:44.393 --> 00:10:46.062
for a lot of guys.

00:10:46.062 --> 00:10:47.355
We came into this bubble with the idea

00:10:47.355 --> 00:10:49.231
that we were gonna be
here for the long haul.

00:10:49.231 --> 00:10:50.441
We were prepared for the long haul.

00:10:50.441 --> 00:10:53.611
I think our families were
prepared for that process as well.

00:10:53.611 --> 00:10:56.697
So, we followed through
with them coming here.

00:10:56.697 --> 00:10:57.990
Everybody has their support system.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:00.076
But it's gonna be important
coming down the stretch,

00:11:00.076 --> 00:11:01.827
you know, just to have some people.

00:11:02.828 --> 00:11:04.705
The lack of fans in the
building, for us to have

00:11:04.705 --> 00:11:06.207
a group of people that's
here for us, that's great.

00:11:06.207 --> 00:11:08.376
- [Taylor:] But does the
energy feel different now

00:11:08.376 --> 00:11:09.543
as opposed to before the families?

00:11:09.543 --> 00:11:10.878
- No, you still can't hear 'em for real.

00:11:10.878 --> 00:11:12.672
- [Taylor, laughing:] OK.
- It's good to have 'em here, though.

00:11:12.672 --> 00:11:14.048
- [Taylor:] All right. Thank you.

00:11:14.048 --> 00:11:16.801
[Cheering]

00:11:23.224 --> 00:11:28.229
[Whistle blowing]
[Cheering]

00:11:34.193 --> 00:11:35.528
Double OT, baby!

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.033
[Chanting]

00:11:41.951 --> 00:11:44.286
[Whistle blowing]

00:11:51.836 --> 00:11:54.380
OK, so I might just be hype,

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:57.091
but that was one of the
best playoff games ever!

00:11:57.091 --> 00:12:01.053
Double OT. What a showing from
the Raptors and the Celtics.

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:04.140
Even had a bit of a, like,
a weird scuffle, scrum,

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.767
in the end when they were
headed to the locker room.

00:12:06.767 --> 00:12:07.977
I recorded that.

00:12:07.977 --> 00:12:12.440
I also asked Jaylen
Brown what that even was.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.607
Hey, Jaylen, as you guys were heading

00:12:13.607 --> 00:12:14.483
back to the locker room,

00:12:14.483 --> 00:12:16.610
it seemed like the
teams were exchanging words.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:17.695
You know, what happened there?

00:12:17.695 --> 00:12:18.821
What was that about?

00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:24.702
- [Exhaling] You know, a lot of emotions
and things like that

00:12:24.702 --> 00:12:26.370
swirling, et cetera.

00:12:27.496 --> 00:12:30.207
I ain't gonna really speak
on that too much, you know?

00:12:31.125 --> 00:12:34.462
But, you know, it's a lot of emotions,
and it's an intense series.

00:12:34.462 --> 00:12:36.964
So, you know, things like
that tend to happen.

00:12:36.964 --> 00:12:38.382
- Packing up the spot.

00:12:40.301 --> 00:12:42.470
Saying goodbye to the bubble.

00:12:44.346 --> 00:12:45.347
Adios.

00:12:47.391 --> 00:12:49.226
I'm actually kinda sad.

00:12:50.853 --> 00:12:53.481
Game 4, Lakers-Rockets.

00:12:53.481 --> 00:12:56.233
It's my final game of the bubble.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:58.694
I'm so sad.

00:12:58.694 --> 00:13:03.574
But right now, it's 26-22,
Lakers. A lot of game left.

00:13:05.117 --> 00:13:07.161
Let's see what happens.

00:13:07.161 --> 00:13:11.499
[Shouting]
[Cheering]

00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:14.251
[Chanting]

00:13:19.215 --> 00:13:21.967
[Cheering]

00:13:27.389 --> 00:13:31.143
Final night in the bubble.

00:13:31.143 --> 00:13:32.978
So I wrote an Instagram caption,

00:13:32.978 --> 00:13:35.773
but I feel like I need to
share it first with you all,

00:13:35.773 --> 00:13:37.441
the viewers of the vlog.

00:13:38.692 --> 00:13:40.861
All right, so this is what it says:

00:13:40.861 --> 00:13:43.072
In the morning, I leave the bubble.

00:13:43.072 --> 00:13:45.032
Heading to St. Louis to be with my family

00:13:45.032 --> 00:13:48.494
as we remember the amazing
life of my Uncle Lou.

00:13:48.494 --> 00:13:51.205
These two months have
been the most memorable

00:13:51.205 --> 00:13:53.707
and important moments of my career.

00:13:53.707 --> 00:13:54.583
Hello, world!

00:13:55.501 --> 00:13:57.086
I'm here!

00:13:57.086 --> 00:13:59.505
There are a few times in life
that you get to be a part

00:13:59.505 --> 00:14:01.841
of a first and an only.

00:14:01.841 --> 00:14:05.553
- I caught myself.
[Laughing]

00:14:05.553 --> 00:14:07.888
- This layered experience
came in the midst

00:14:07.888 --> 00:14:10.599
of a country dealing with systemic racism,

00:14:10.599 --> 00:14:14.395
police brutality and
a devastating pandemic.

00:14:14.395 --> 00:14:16.772
Players sat out. Players
used their voices.

00:14:16.772 --> 00:14:19.233
Players battled with an
array of deep emotions

00:14:19.233 --> 00:14:21.402
while still competing for a championship.

00:14:21.402 --> 00:14:23.863
Every day, I asked myself how to best

00:14:23.863 --> 00:14:26.282
do my job to convey this story.

00:14:26.282 --> 00:14:27.908
Being deliberate with questions,

00:14:27.908 --> 00:14:30.536
taking videos of sounds
and moments that mattered,

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:34.915
but also capturing the joy and
levity that presented itself.

00:14:34.915 --> 00:14:37.877
[Upbeat organ music]

00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:41.213
- [Announcer:] Three points Lakers!

00:14:41.213 --> 00:14:43.549
- One day, people will make movies

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:45.634
and write books about this time.

00:14:45.634 --> 00:14:47.845
This was history.

00:14:47.845 --> 00:14:49.763
I feel blessed and thankful

00:14:49.763 --> 00:14:52.099
that I was able to record history.

00:14:53.267 --> 00:14:54.268
[Getting choked up] Whew.

00:14:54.268 --> 00:14:57.646
And I'm so thankful to all
of you that followed along.

00:14:59.231 --> 00:15:01.775
But there are so many
more games to be played

00:15:01.775 --> 00:15:04.069
and more changes to be made.

00:15:04.069 --> 00:15:05.404
Peace and love.

